Exercise: sa-containers-review (chapter 21 lab)

Work on servera as the user student (log in with ssh; a real login is needed
for user services). Use sudo only where noted. Install podman if needed.

Image
 1. Create ~/portal with a file index.html that contains: Portal is up
 2. Write ~/portal/Containerfile: it starts FROM
    registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/httpd-24 and copies index.html to
    /var/www/html/index.html. Build the image as localhost/portal:1.

Service
 3. Write the Quadlet file ~/.config/containers/systemd/portal.container
    for that image: publish 8080:8080, Restart=always, and
    WantedBy=default.target in the Install section.
 4. Reload the user systemd and start portal.service. The container is
    named systemd-portal and must be running.

After a reboot, and for other hosts
 5. Enable lingering for student (sudo loginctl enable-linger student).
 6. Open 8080/tcp permanently in the firewall and reload.
 7. Check from serverb: curl http://servera:8080/

On workstation
 8. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-containers-review
